sg-session (0.1.0-24) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The first-run setup (OOBE) at an installed machine's first boot, in the
    login screen's place: region, keyboard (and a second layout), network,
    the owner's account when there is none, privacy (no diagnostic data),
    an optional web browser. sg-oobed (root, only while pending) validates
    and applies; each user's HKCU gets the choices at first sign-in.
  * Every compositor gets the keyboard from /etc/default/keyboard.
  * Gate: make test-oobe.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:49:56 -0700

sg-session (0.1.0-23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The lock screen shows the picture chosen in Settings > Personalization >
    Lock screen, with the time and date at the bottom left (Windows 10's
    curtain); a key, click or the wheel lifts it to the sign-in pane over the
    blurred, dimmed picture (or the plain colour when "show on the sign-in
    screen" is off), with the account's initial. The login screen has the
    curtain over the system's picture. The key that lifts it is typed.
  * sg-settingsctl lockscreen: publishes the user's choice, as the user,
    into /var/lib/stained-glass/lockscreen (tmpfiles, 1733); sg-lockd stages
    it for the lock UI only if it is the session user's own regular file
    (no symlinks), a JPEG/PNG/BMP/GIF, at most 32 MB -- copied from the
    checked descriptor.
  * Gate: make test-lockpic; make test-lock checks the picture is staged,
    shown on the lock screen's X server, and removed after unlocking.

