sg-session (0.1.0-22) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-settingsctl: sleep-caps (logind CanSuspend/CanHibernate) and sleep
    suspend|hibernate (lock, then systemctl), for Start's Sleep; swayidle runs
    for the whole session and locks before any sleep (before-sleep
    sg-lockctl LOCK, after-resume wlopm --on), whatever the timeouts.

