sg-session (0.1.0-20) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-settingsctl: the native half of Settings (sg-shell's sg-settings),
    as the signed-in user -- sound devices, defaults, volumes and mute
    (PipeWire through pactl), Bluetooth (bluez: power, scan, pair, connect,
    disconnect, remove), the compositor's display modes and scale
    (wlr-randr), night light (wlsunset at a fixed temperature), Power &
    sleep's screen and sleep timers (swayidle; wlopm for the screen), and
    apt's pending updates. Answers through --out files for Windows programs;
    inputs validated before any tool runs; choices kept in
    ~/.config/stained-glass/settings.json and applied again by
    sg-run-explorer at every sign-in (session-start).
  * Recommends wlr-randr, wlsunset, swayidle, wlopm, bluez.
  * Gate: test/settingsctl-test.py (in make lint).

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:55:17 -0700

sg-session (0.1.0-19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-sysinfo: the administrative tools' Linux side -- devices (Device
    Manager: PCI/USB/network/disks/sound/input/monitors/CPUs with drivers,
    kernel modules and sg-drivers' "no driver" recommendations), disks and
    volumes with drive letters and unallocated space (Disk Management),
    Stained Glass's systemd units (Services), local users and groups, Samba
    shares, a hardware/OS summary (System Information), processes and
    connections (Resource Monitor), cleanup categories (Disk Cleanup).
    Windows programs reach it through `sg-sysinfo --bridge`.
  * sg-sysinfod (socket-activated, root): the Stained Glass journal for
    anyone with a Windows session; mount, unmount, drive letters, format,
    Samba sessions and system cleanup for administrators, refusing the
    system disk and volumes in use.
  * Gate: test/sysinfo-test.py (in make lint).

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:48:54 -0700

